85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Synchronization is implemented with mutexes and condition variables. In addition, the system includes a monitoring thread for deadlock detection using a wait-for graph approach. Runtime statistics such as throughput, blocking time, waiting time, deadlock frequency, and CPU utilization are also recorded. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (The project satisfies the assignment requirements including concurrent execution, bounded shared buffers, synchronization support, deadlock monitoring, configuration-based topology, logging, and performance experiments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 57 0 R
/T (Design Approach)
/E (Design Approach)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The project implements a modular and scalable multi-threaded architecture designed to simulate complex data flow scenarios. The design is centered around three fundamental pillars: )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 236 0 R
/E (Dynamic Resource Mapping: Instead of hard-coded structures, the system uses a Configuration Parser to build a network of named buffers and threads at runtime. This allows for the flexible definition of buffer capacities and thread roles \(Producer, Consumer, or Pipeline Worker\) via external config files.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Thread Context Abstraction: Every thread is decoupled from the main logic using a Thread Context structure. This structure encapsulates all operational data, such as timing intervals and buffer references, allowing the same generic code to handle diverse tasks depending on its assigned context.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 238 0 R
/E (Decentralized Synchronization: To maximize concurrency, each named buffer operates as an independent synchronization unit. By utilizing localized POSIX Mutexes and Condition Variables \(not_full, not_empty\), the design ensures that threads only block when their specific resource is unavailable, preventing global system bottlenecks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 239 0 R
/E (Active Graph-Based Monitoring: The system incorporates a dedicated Deadlock Monitor that maintains a real-time state of the simulation. By tracking "held" and "requested" resources for every thread, it constructs a Wait-for Graph to proactively detect circular dependencies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 240 0 R
/E (Graceful Termination: Reliability is ensured through a controlled shutdown protocol. Upon reaching the runtime limit, a global broadcast signal forces all sleeping threads to wake up and exit cleanly, ensuring all allocated resources are released.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (The implementation is divided into separate modules responsible for configuration parsing, buffer management, producer and consumer logic, deadlock detection, metrics, and logging. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (The runtime state is represented through a shared simulation_t structure containing: shared buffers runtime metrics synchronization resources )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E ( Report logger instance monitoring information Each thread receives a thread_context_t structure storing timing configuration, identity, and related input/output buffers. This makes the system configurable and avoids hardcoded dependencies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
